blurb = "Depicts travelers descending a steep mountain path in Kōzuke Province (present-day Gunma prefecture). In the background is the naka-no-take (\"middle peak\") of Mount Myōgi, known for its unusual rock formations and steep, jagged spires.

This is not to be confused with Mount Nakano in Hokkaidō, which is also sometimes called naka-no-take."
